OL,3,GNEWSALeader of flag campaign pleads not
OL,4,Aguilty to offences
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe leader of a group responsible for
OL,7,Fraising Union Jack and St George's
OL,8,FCross flags across England has pleaded
OL,9,Fnot guilty to a string of offences
OL,10,Fincluding racially aggravated
OL,11,Fharassment, threatening behaviour and
OL,12,Fassault.
OL,14,FRyan Bridge, 45, of Bromsgrove,
OL,15,FWorcestershire, co-founded the
OL,16,Fnationalist group Raise the Colours
OL,17,Fwhich has been hoisting flags on
OL,18,Flamp-posts since August last year.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,338,330,200,160,0,100
